<body>

<!-- HEADER -->
<header class="report-header">
  <div class="header-inner">
    <div class="header-badge">Financial Analysis Report</div>
    <h1 class="header-title">Nike Inc. (NKE)<br>Historical Stock Performance</h1>
    <p class="header-subtitle">A 26-year retrospective of price trends, volatility, and trading dynamics (2000–2026)</p>
    <div class="header-meta">
      <span>&#128197; Dataset Period: Jan 3, 2000 – Jan 30, 2026</span>
      <span>&#128200; 6,559 Trading Days</span>
      <span>&#127775; Audience: Long-Term Investors</span>
      <span>&#128338; Generated: April 21, 2026</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- TOC -->
<nav class="toc-bar" aria-label="Report sections">
  <div class="toc-inner">
    <a class="toc-link" href="#executive-summary">Executive Summary</a>
    <a class="toc-link" href="#price-trend">Price Trend</a>
    <a class="toc-link" href="#volatility">Volatility &amp; Risk</a>
    <a class="toc-link" href="#volume">Volume Patterns</a>
    <a class="toc-link" href="#annual">Annual Performance</a>
    <a class="toc-link" href="#takeaways">Key Takeaways</a>
  </div>
</nav>

<main>
<div class="container">

<!-- ===== SECTION 1: EXECUTIVE SUMMARY ===== -->
<section class="section" id="executive-summary">
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-label">Section 1</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Executive Summary</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">Key performance indicators and top-line findings across the full 26-year study period.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- KPI Dashboard -->
  <div class="kpi-grid" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
    <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color:#16a34a;">
      <div class="kpi-label">Cumulative Return</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">+1,282%</div>
      <div class="kpi-desc">Jan 3, 2000 → Jan 30, 2026<br>$4.47 → $61.81 (adj.)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color:#2563eb;">
      <div class="kpi-label">CAGR</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">10.60%</div>
      <div class="kpi-desc">Compound annual growth rate over 26.08 years</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color:#dc2626;">
      <div class="kpi-label">Max Drawdown</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">−68.5%</div>
      <div class="kpi-desc">Nov 5, 2021 peak ($166.25) → Apr 8, 2025 trough ($52.31)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color:#d97706;">
      <div class="kpi-label">Ann. Volatility</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">31.2%</div>
      <div class="kpi-desc">Std. dev. of daily returns × √252, full period</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color:#7c3aed;">
      <div class="kpi-label">Avg Daily Volume</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">10.67M</div>
      <div class="kpi-desc">Mean shares/day across all 6,559 trading sessions</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Summary narrative -->
  <div class="chart-wrap" style="padding:28px 28px 22px;">
    <p style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--gray-700);margin-bottom:14px;">
      Over the 26-year period from January 2000 through January 2026, Nike Inc. delivered a cumulative adjusted-price return of
      <strong>+1,282%</strong>, compounding at <strong>10.60% annually</strong> — a performance firmly above the long-run historical average of large-cap U.S. equities.
      The journey was far from linear: NKE endured multiple severe drawdowns including a 68.5% peak-to-trough collapse from its 2021 all-time high of <strong>$166.25</strong> to an April 2025 multi-year low of <strong>$52.31</strong>.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--gray-700);margin-bottom:14px;">
      Three distinct structural epochs define the stock's history: a <em>volatile base-building phase</em> in the early 2000s, a
      powerful <em>secular bull market</em> from 2003 through 2021 interrupted only briefly by the 2008 GFC and 2020 COVID crash,
      and a <em>prolonged correction/distribution phase</em> beginning in late 2021 that has persisted through early 2026.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--gray-700);">
      All data in this report is sourced directly from the 6,559-row daily trading dataset covering January 3, 2000 through January 30, 2026.
      Prices are adjusted for stock splits and dividends.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Milestone table -->
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-body">
      <div class="chart-title">Key Milestones</div>
      <div class="chart-subtitle" style="margin-bottom:16px;">Significant price events over the study period</div>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Event</th><th>Date</th><th class="num">Adj. Close Price</th><th>Significance</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>All-Time Low (adj.)</td><td>Feb 25, 2000</td><td class="num neg">$2.47</td><td>Post-dot-com collapse, early-decade pessimism</td></tr>
            <tr><td>First Close (dataset)</td><td>Jan 3, 2000</td><td class="num">$4.47</td><td>Baseline for all return calculations</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Decade Close – 2000s</td><td>Dec 31, 2009</td><td class="num pos">$13.41</td><td>+200% from 2000 low; post-GFC recovery</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Decade Close – 2010s</td><td>Dec 31, 2019</td><td class="num pos">$93.45</td><td>+597% from decade start; peak growth era</td></tr>
            <tr><td>COVID-19 Low</td><td>Mar 2020 (approx.)</td><td class="num neg">~$55.50</td><td>Rapid 38% intra-year drop, swift recovery</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>All-Time High (adj.)</strong></td><td><strong>Nov 5, 2021</strong></td><td class="num pos"><strong>$166.25</strong></td><td>Peak valuation; consumer boom, post-COVID</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Max Drawdown Trough</td><td>Apr 8, 2025</td><td class="num neg">$52.31</td><td>−68.5% from ATH; structural correction</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Last Close (dataset)</td><td>Jan 30, 2026</td><td class="num">$61.81</td><td>Partial recovery from 2025 lows</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== SECTION 2: PRICE TREND ===== -->
<section class="section" id="price-trend">
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-label">Section 2</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Long-Term Price Trend Analysis</h2>
