  <div class="insight-grid">
    <div class="insight-card" style="--ins-color:#16a34a;">
      <div class="insight-icon">&#128200;</div>
      <div class="insight-title">Strong Long-Run Compounder</div>
      <div class="insight-body">A 10.60% CAGR over 26 years confirms NKE as an above-average compounder among large-cap consumer equities. A $10,000 investment at the Jan 2000 open would be worth approximately $138,200 at the Jan 2026 close — before any dividend reinvestment. For patient, buy-and-hold investors, NKE rewarded conviction.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="insight-card" style="--ins-color:#dc2626;">
      <div class="insight-icon">&#9888;</div>
      <div class="insight-title">Drawdowns Are Severe &amp; Extended</div>
      <div class="insight-body">The 68.5% maximum drawdown (2021–2025) is not an anomaly — the stock also suffered through the dot-com era collapse and the GFC. Investors with shorter horizons or low drawdown tolerance would have faced significant realized losses. Position sizing and time-horizon alignment are critical risk management levers for NKE exposure.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="insight-card" style="--ins-color:#2563eb;">
      <div class="insight-icon">&#128337;</div>
      <div class="insight-title">Volatility Cycles With Macro Regimes</div>
      <div class="insight-body">NKE's realized volatility oscillates between 15–25% in calm periods and 40–56% during stress. Stress episodes correlate closely with global crises (2000–2002, 2008–2009, 2020, 2022–2025). Investors entering during high-volatility periods historically captured stronger forward returns, consistent with crisis = opportunity dynamics.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="insight-card" style="--ins-color:#d97706;">
      <div class="insight-icon">&#128202;</div>
      <div class="insight-title">Volume as a Sentiment Barometer</div>
      <div class="insight-body">Trading volume provides confirmatory signals. High volume during price declines (2008, 2022–2025) signals institutional distribution and typically precedes further weakness. Low volume during rallies (2013–2019) can reflect a healthy low-supply, buy-and-hold environment. The return of high volume since 2022 in a downtrending market is a caution flag.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="insight-card" style="--ins-color:#7c3aed;">
      <div class="insight-icon">&#128101;</div>
      <div class="insight-title">Decade Risk Is Underappreciated</div>
      <div class="insight-body">The 2020–2026 partial decade illustrates that even elite compounders can experience multi-year negative-return periods. Investors who entered at the 2021 ATH have lost more than half their capital through early 2026. Valuation discipline — avoiding entry at peak multiples — meaningfully affects realized investor returns versus stock returns.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="insight-card" style="--ins-color:#0891b2;">
      <div class="insight-icon">&#127919;</div>
      <div class="insight-title">Current Setup (as of Jan 2026)</div>
      <div class="insight-body">At $61.81, NKE trades at roughly 37% of its 2021 ATH. The stock has stabilized above the Apr 2025 trough of $52.31. Historically, NKE has recovered strongly from multi-year drawdowns. Whether the current correction phase is complete or ongoing requires fundamental analysis beyond this price-only dataset — but the historical precedent for long-run recovery is well-established.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

